WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.083
An unrooted tree becomes a hierarchy as soon as you pick an arbitrary node as the root.

00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:10.767
Information then flows cleanly from leaves upward to their parents.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:16.360
Establish parent-child edges first so transitions never revisit the parent node.

00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:23.691
Deep trees with two hundred thousand nodes can trigger Python's recursion limit and high function-call overhead.

00:00:23.691 --> 00:00:30.056
Build a breadth-first or stack traversal list first, then iterate through that list in reverse order.

00:00:30.056 --> 00:00:34.593
Reverse traversal guarantees every child is processed before its parent.

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:41.438
At each node u, accumulate child DP values into states such as taking u versus skipping u.

00:00:41.438 --> 00:00:49.324
For tree diameter or maximum independent set, each child contributes in constant time to its parent's state.

00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:53.267
The whole bottom-up pass finishes in linear O(N) time.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:01:00.585
When a problem asks for the answer assuming every node takes a turn as the root, run a second top-down pass.

00:01:00.585 --> 00:01:07.733
Pass the parent's outside contribution down to each child using prefix and suffix products of sibling results.

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:11.178
All N root answers are computed in total linear time.
